      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(memory-wiki): strip fenced code and inline code before wikilink extraction",
        "body": "Related: #97945\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where `openclaw wiki lint` could still report false `broken-wikilink` warnings for `[[...]]` text inside CommonMark code regions, including tilde fences, longer fences, fenced blocks inside lists or blockquotes, and multiline code spans.\n\nThe earlier masking on `main` handles simple backtick fences and single-line inline code, but ad hoc regex/scanner variants can either leak code text or hide genuine prose links around invalid or multi-backtick delimiters.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMemory Wiki now uses `mdast-util-from-markdown` to identify `code` and `inlineCode` source ranges, masks only those ranges, and then runs the existing wikilink and Markdown-link extraction logic unchanged.\n\nThis keeps parsing at the extractor boundary while delegating CommonMark fence, container, and code-span rules to the repository's existing parser stack. Link normalization, related-block filtering, frontmatter handling, and resolver behavior are unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMemory Wiki lint output no longer includes code-origin false positives for standard CommonMark code regions, while genuine broken links in surrounding prose remain visible.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/memory-wiki/src/markdown.test.ts extensions/memory-wiki/src/lint.test.ts`\n  - 2 files passed\n  - 35 tests passed\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check extensions/memory-wiki/src/markdown.ts extensions/memory-wiki/src/markdown.test.ts extensions/memory-wiki/src/lint.test.ts extensions/memory-wiki/package.json pnpm-lock.yaml`\n  - clean\n- Focused direct probes cover invalid backtick info strings, unmatched backtick runs, blockquote/list fences, multiline code spans, and separate multi-backtick spans; each preserves only the real prose link.\n- Structured Codex autoreview against current `origin/main`: clean, no actionable findings.\n\nLocal oxlint could not run after the merge from current `main` because this worktree intentionally shares an older dependency tree that lacks the newly configured oxlint rule. Exact-head CI and the external merge preflight are the authoritative toolchain gates.\n",
